						"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "You do, and no third party. The Vectis Mail model is custody: because you run the server, your messages sit in your own Postgres and IMAP store, wherever you deploy — no external provider holds your mail, scans it, or can be compelled to hand it over. Mail in transit is protected by TLS. With a hosted suite your mail lives on the vendor's infrastructure under a policy you can inspect but not control; with Vectis Mail the boundary is your own server, so the question becomes 'where did you deploy it' rather than 'do you trust the vendor's attestation.'" }
